From 44a828debfa3555c0906934471d8d02be935808f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Buldygin <froooks@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 16:54:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: sc3336: fix double clk_disable_unprepare in
 power_off

__sc3336_power_off() calls clk_disable_unprepare(sc3336->xvclk) twice:
once unconditionally at the top of the function, and again a few lines
later after toggling pwdn_gpio. The clock core WARNs on the second call
("mclk_ref_mipi0 already disabled" / "already unprepared") with a full
backtrace, which is emitted on every power-off -- including when sc3336
loses a probe race against another sensor sharing the same mipi refclk
(see the DT change enabling rockchip,camera_default pinctrl for
sc3336/mis5001 auto-detection) and never gets to stream.

Drop the second, redundant call. The first call already unconditionally
disables/unprepares the clock before the is_thunderboot early-return
check, so behaviour is unchanged for both the thunderboot and normal
power-off paths -- only the duplicate disable (and its WARNING) is
removed.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/i2c/sc3336.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/sc3336.c b/drivers/media/i2c/sc3336.c
index aae6bcaf5a6a..b44a302f6575 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/sc3336.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/sc3336.c
@@ -1193,7 +1193,6 @@ static void __sc3336_power_off(struct sc3336 *sc3336)
 
 	if (!IS_ERR(sc3336->pwdn_gpio))
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sc3336->pwdn_gpio, 0);
-	clk_disable_unprepare(sc3336->xvclk);
 	if (!IS_ERR(sc3336->reset_gpio))
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sc3336->reset_gpio, 0);
 	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(sc3336->pins_sleep)) {
-- 
